# ESP-IDF build output (regenerated by `idf.py build`)
build/
**/build/
# per-variant build dirs from run.ps1 (build_root_wormhole_tree, build_victim_wormhole_tree_B, ...)
build_*/
**/build_*/

# build_all_variants.ps1's compile-check dirs. These are NOT called build_*:
# they were deliberately shortened to bcr/bcc/bcba/bcbv/bcwa/bcwb (sep. 22, 2026)
# because the long `build_check_<Name>` paths pushed ninja's object paths past
# Windows MAX_PATH and failed in the bootloader subproject. That rename also
# walked them straight out of the `build_*/` rule above, leaving ~8,500 files of
# build output untracked-but-not-ignored, one `git add -A` away from the repo.
# Keep this list in sync with the $variants table in build_all_variants.ps1.
bc[a-z]*/
**/bc[a-z]*/

# sdkconfig backups / generated headers
sdkconfig.old
**/sdkconfig.old

# sniffer_node's generated config: IDF defaults + its sdkconfig.defaults are the
# whole config, and a tracked copy would churn between IDF 5.3 and 5.5 laptops.
sniffer_node/sdkconfig
sniffer_node/dependencies.lock

# CLion / CMake
cmake-build-*/
.idea/

# ── Host-side export output (tools/exports/) ────────────────────────────────
# RAW CAPTURES ARE TRACKED ON PURPOSE. They are the thesis's primary evidence
# and are irreplaceable — the boards get wiped for the next run — so the team
# needs them on GitHub (see commits 69e6057 / 8200955, "for team visibility").
# ~6 MB for the whole current matrix. What we do NOT track:
#
#   _archive/     superseded runs kept only for provenance (~46 MB). preprocess.py
#                 writes one per LEAF folder, so this needs **, not a bare prefix.
#   archive/      the same thing hand-made; the team's real archive lives at
#                 <repo>/archive/<date>_<label>/ and is tracked normally.
#   trimmed/      derived from raw by trim_run.py; regenerate, don't store
#   manifest.json rewritten by validate_integrity.py on every run
datasets/exports/**/_archive/
datasets/exports/**/archive/
datasets/exports/**/trimmed/
datasets/exports/**/manifest.json

# Stray exports/ folders — NOT real output folders. All four host tools used to
# default their output/scan dir to a bare "exports" resolved against the SHELL'S
# CWD, so running one from the wrong directory created and/or scanned an
# exports/ there. This happened three times for real:
#
#   exports/                 (repo root)   committed in 8200955
#   root_node/exports/       a whole baseline-tree run written here by
#   child_node/exports/      export_logs.py, because that is where you already
#                            stand for `idf.py set-target` / flashing
#
# export_logs.py was the damaging one — it WRITES captures, so irreplaceable
# data landed somewhere no analysis command looks. All four defaults now
# resolve next to their own script, so this should never recur; these rules
# stay as a backstop. Real captures live in tools/exports/.
/exports/
/root_node/exports/
/child_node/exports/

# Host-side analysis output (regenerated by run.ps1 -Analyze / the M6-M8 scripts).
# Only the .gitkeep scaffold under analysis/<attack>/<topology>_topology/ is tracked;
# the derived datasets/plots are not.
datasets/analysis/**/windowed_dataset.csv
datasets/analysis/**/feature_table.csv
datasets/analysis/**/eda_output/

# This laptop's latest SD-import batch (tools/ImportBatch.ps1) - what push/pull
# lists show green. Per-laptop state, never shared.
.last_import_batch.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Archived runs (archive/<date>/exports|analysis/...) — same tracking policy as the
# live tools/exports/ + analysis/ trees above: raw captures + run_ledger.csv are
# evidence and stay tracked; derived/regenerable artifacts don't.
datasets/archive/**/exports/**/trimmed/
datasets/archive/**/exports/**/manifest.json
datasets/archive/**/analysis/**/windowed_dataset.csv
datasets/archive/**/analysis/**/feature_table.csv
datasets/archive/**/analysis/**/eda_output/

# OS junk
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store


how to run esp32.txt


# Raw packet captures — large, kept local only (GitHub 100MB cap)
PCAP/
*.pcap
